.TH SWAYDESK-LOCK 1 2026-11-14 "swaydesk 0.1.5" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-lock \- lock screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-lock
\-\-notify\-fd N
.br
.B swaydesk\-lock
\-\-blur
.SH DESCRIPTION
The lock screen, through ext\-session\-lock\-v1 (gtk4\-layer\-shell 1.2 or newer). Do not run it directly: the sway\-lock helper starts it through its supervisor, which falls back to the lock in Python (sway\-lock\-gtk, on Debian and Ubuntu) and then to gtklock if it fails, and hands the lock to another locker if it exits without unlocking. The password field is on every monitor, takes dead keys through GTK's simple input method (never an input method daemon), and PAM checks the password with the swaydesk\-lock service.
.PP
Without the lock support in gtk4\-layer\-shell, it exits 1 and sway\-lock uses the next locker.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-notify\-fd N
Write L to the file descriptor N when locked, F if another client already locked, and U after the unlock.
.TP
.B \-\-blur
Generate the blurred background of each monitor in advance (also when run as sway\-lock\-blur); without Sway or a wallpaper, do nothing and exit 0.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit 0 if the installed gtk4\-layer\-shell supports locking, 1 if not.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/swaydesk-lock
The PAM service used to check the password (only \fBauth include login\fR, like swaylock's). Without it, the
swaylock service, \fI/etc/pam.d/swaylock\fR, is used.
.TP
.I ~/.config/swaydesk/config.toml
The desktop configuration: language, accent color, GTK and icon themes, folder color, file manager, weather location and holidays.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pam (8),
.BR swaydesk (7),
.BR gtklock (1)
